17:30:23	./sim-root/runs/r12/edgeops	update edgeops-mol-h7z --description The runbook sizes capacity for one region gone, not two. Before anything is pulled from us-west-2:

- No other region has a node out of the pool, in maintenance, or in an open incident. docs/oncall.md defines the severities.
- Record the error rate and connection count for us-west-2 now. The restore step is judged against this baseline.
- Count the nodes in us-west-2. README.md says eleven nodes in four regions, but terraform/nodes.tf declares one node per region. If us-west-2 has more than one, drain them one at a time and check capacity after each.

## Acceptance Criteria
- No other region is drained, in maintenance, or in an open incident, checked on the day of the work.
- The baseline error rate and connection count for us-west-2 are written on this step.
- The node count in us-west-2 is known. If it does not match terraform/nodes.tf, that is filed as its own issue.

17:30:24	./sim-root/runs/r12/edgeops	update edgeops-mol-1yt --description Run once, from the repo root, after the capacity step is done:

    ops/drain.sh UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node

drain.sh runs `edgectl pool remove UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node`, then `edgectl wait-drain UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node --timeout 300`, and prints "drained UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node" on success. edgectl is the fleet's control CLI and is not in this repo.

## Acceptance Criteria
- ops/drain.sh UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node exited zero and printed "drained UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node".
- UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node is out of the anycast pool.

17:30:24	./sim-root/runs/r12/edgeops	update edgeops-mol-1cy --description drain.sh waits up to 300 seconds and exits non-zero on timeout (set -e), so nothing after it runs. Continue only if it printed "drained UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node" and exited zero.

If it fails, stop. The node is out of the pool but still holds connections, and replacing it now drops them. Get the on-call to decide whether to wait longer.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Connections on UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node reached zero inside the 300 second timeout.
- If they did not, the on-call decision is written on this step and no replacement was started.

17:30:25	./sim-root/runs/r12/edgeops	update edgeops-mol-41h --description A kernel patch is an image roll. Nothing is changed by hand on a node (README.md): the node is replaced by one built on the patched image.

1. Confirm the patched image UNRESOLVED-patched-kernel-image exists in the image build. The repo does not hold the id. If UNRESOLVED-patched-kernel-image is empty, this is a reboot or a resize, not an image roll.
2. Find out whether the edge provider adds a new node to the anycast pool when it is created. create_before_destroy makes the replacement exist before the drained node is destroyed. If the pool takes it at create, stop: it would take traffic before the verify step.
3. Plan from terraform/, with the replacement forced to this node only:

    cd terraform
    terraform plan -out=patch-us-west-2.tfplan -var='image_overrides={"us-west-2"="UNRESOLVED-patched-kernel-image"}' -replace='edge_node.fleet["us-west-2"]'

4. Read the plan. It must replace edge_node.fleet["us-west-2"] and change nothing else. If it touches another region, or shows an in-place update instead of a replacement, stop.
5. Apply the saved plan and nothing else: terraform apply patch-us-west-2.tfplan. Then delete the plan file.

-var replaces the whole map, so list every region that has an override, not only this one. terraform 1.6 or newer is required (terraform/main.tf). The s3 state backend credentials come from the secret manager (docs/secrets.md), not from the repo.

## Acceptance Criteria
- The plan replaced only edge_node.fleet["us-west-2"] and nothing else.
- The applied image is UNRESOLVED-patched-kernel-image, or the image is unchanged for a reboot or a resize.
- The saved plan file is deleted.

17:30:25	./sim-root/runs/r12/edgeops	update edgeops-mol-pnz --description Before the node takes traffic, check that the replacement is on the patched kernel and healthy. The repo has no command for this yet. Confirm the edgectl subcommand with `edgectl --help` first, then record the kernel version and the health result on this step.

If either is wrong, do not return the node to the pool. Remove us-west-2 from image_overrides, plan and replace again the same way, and see docs/runbook.md for rollback.

## Acceptance Criteria
- The replacement reports the patched kernel version, written on this step.
- Its health check passes.
- UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node is still out of the anycast pool.

17:30:26	./sim-root/runs/r12/edgeops	update edgeops-mol-zx7 --description Put UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node back in the pool. drain.sh only removes nodes, and the repo has no script that adds them back. Confirm the edgectl pool subcommand with `edgectl pool --help`, then run it for UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node.

Watch the error rate and connection count in us-west-2 against the baseline from the capacity step. Wait fifteen minutes and check again before any other region has maintenance (docs/runbook.md: fifteen minutes between regions).

## Acceptance Criteria
- UNRESOLVED-us-west-2-node is back in the anycast pool and taking traffic.
- Error rate and connection count in us-west-2 stayed within the baseline for fifteen minutes.
- No other region had maintenance in those fifteen minutes.

